BEGIN_PGML We call the number of edges incident to a particular vertex (i.e., the number of edges "coming out of" the vertex) the degree of the vertex. A list of the degrees of all the vertices in non-increasing order is called a degree sequence for the graph. Find the degree sequence for each graph.
[`G_1`] has degree sequence: [_]{List(3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3)}{25}.
[`G_2`] has degree sequence: [_]{List(3,3,2,2,2,2)}{25}.
[`G_3`] has degree sequence: [_]{List(3,3,2,2,2,2)}{25}.
[`G_4`] has degree sequence: [_]{List(2, 2, 2, 2, 1 ,1)}{25}.
END_PGML
